 r←PrepareHtmlPageForDependencies_ dep;id;registry
⍝ Returns one row of the list of dependencies; see `PrepareHtmlPageForDependencies`.
⍝ A line in a dependencies file names a package ID, possibly preceded by the alias it is loaded
⍝ under ("A@aplteam-APLTreeUtils2-1.1.1") or by the URL of the Registry it comes from.
⍝ * A dependency in this Registry leads to its configuration and says whether it has
⍝   dependencies of its own.
⍝ * One from another Registry is named together with that Registry.
⍝ * One that ought to be in this Registry but is not is just named.
 dep←'^[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*@'⎕R''⊣dep              ⍝ The alias, if any, is of no interest here
 r←'<div class="dep-row">'
 :If '/'∊dep
     id←dep↑⍨-¯1+(⌽dep)⍳'/'
     registry←dep↓⍨-≢id
     r,←'<span class="dep-id">',(EscapeSpecialChars id),'</span><span class="dep-note">from ',(EscapeSpecialChars registry),'</span>'
 :ElseIf F.IsDir G.RegistryPath,dep
     r,←'<a class="dep-id" href="',Reg.VersionOf_REST,'/packages/details/',dep,'">',dep,'</a>'
     :If PackageHasDependencies dep
         r,←'<a class="dep-note" href="',Reg.VersionOf_REST,'/packages/dependencies/',dep,'">its dependencies</a>'
     :Else
         r,←'<span class="dep-note">no dependencies of its own</span>'
     :EndIf
 :Else
     r,←'<span class="dep-id">',(EscapeSpecialChars dep),'</span><span class="dep-note">not in this Registry</span>'
 :EndIf
 r,←'</div>'
⍝Done
